---

8. Input Validation

Validation is implemented before sending information to the AI system.

The system checks:

Required fields

Valid dates

Valid email format where applicable

Empty fields

Invalid values

Excessively long input


If information is missing, the application displays a clear message.

Example:

> Please enter the tenant name before generating the document.




---

9. Backend Development

The Flask backend handles communication between the frontend and AI service.

Backend responsibilities

Receive User Input
       ↓
Validate Input
       ↓
Identify Document Type
       ↓
Prepare AI Prompt
       ↓
Send Request to AI
       ↓
Receive Response
       ↓
Format Response
       ↓
Send Draft to Frontend

The backend keeps sensitive API credentials away from the frontend.


---

10. AI Integration

AI integration is the main development component of LegalEase.

The selected AI service receives a structured prompt containing:

Document type

User information

Required sections

Formatting instructions

Instructions not to invent important facts


Example

Document Type:
Authorization Letter

Person Giving Authorization:
[User information]

Authorized Person:
[User information]

Purpose:
[User information]

Generate a clear structured draft using the
information provided. Do not invent missing
important facts.

The AI then returns the generated draft.


---

11. AI Output Processing

The backend processes the AI response before displaying it.

The system can:

Remove unwanted formatting.

Organize headings.

Separate paragraphs.

Identify missing information.

Prepare the content for document export.


The output is then sent to the preview page.


